# Authentication Settings (ADR-002, design 18.6, issue GH-145)
#
# Leave every VITE_ENTRA_* value blank for local Development: `npm run dev` runs as an
# unauthenticated pass-through shell (no MSAL, no Entra sign-in) -- the backend enforces
# Production separately. A BUILT bundle (`npm run build`) with no ids ALSO needs an explicit
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=Development, which scripts/start.sh and scripts/start.ps1 already set for you; a
# plain `npm run build` with no mode and no ids now fails closed instead of silently shipping an
# unauthenticated pass-through.
#
# For an explicit Entra deployment, set VITE_AUTH_MODE=Entra plus a real, non-placeholder tenant id
# (a GUID -- a directory domain is not accepted) and client id (both fail the build via
# vite.config.ts's auth-mode build guard if only one is set, or if the value looks like a
# placeholder). VITE_ENTRA_API_SCOPE defaults to "access_as_user" (requested as
# api://{VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID}/{scope}) and rarely needs to change.
#
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=Entra
VITE_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=
VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_ENTRA_API_SCOPE=access_as_user
